# Runtime state OpenHands writes into ~/.openhands, which is a symlink to
# .openhands/ here (bin/link-files-nixos). Declarative config stays tracked:
#
#   .openhands/settings.json
#   .openhands/agent-profiles/
#   project/            (Tier 3 — the repo's own .openhands, see project/README.md)
#
# The split is not cosmetic. settings.json is written back by the server through
# persistence/store.py `_atomic_write_json`, which ends in `tmp.replace(path)`.
# That is why ~/.openhands is a DIRECTORY symlink and not a file symlink: the
# rename lands inside this directory, so the tracked file is updated in place
# and shows up as a normal diff. A per-file symlink into the Nix store (or into
# here) would be replaced by a regular file on the first save and silently stop
# being declarative.
#
# Everything below is either a generated credential or state with no reason to
# be reproducible. When adding an entry, prefer "does a fresh host want this
# byte-for-byte?" over "is it small?".

# --- credentials and generated keys ---
# secrets.json holds OPENHANDS_AUTOMATION_API_KEY in plaintext (encrypted only
# when OH_SECRET_KEY is set, which this repo deliberately does not set — there
# is no agenix/sops here, so a committed key would be worse than a generated
# one). The agent-canvas/*.txt files are the 48-byte keys the launcher
# auto-generates and persists across restarts.
.openhands/secrets.json
.openhands/agent-canvas/api-key.txt
.openhands/agent-canvas/automation-kv-secret.txt
.openhands/agent-canvas/secret-key.txt
.openhands/provider-connections/

# --- conversation and session state ---
.openhands/agent-canvas/dev_conversations/
.openhands/agent-canvas/bash_events/
.openhands/agent-canvas/storage/
.openhands/agent-canvas/workspaces/
.openhands/agent-canvas/tmux/
.openhands/agent-canvas/logs/

# --- automation service database ---
.openhands/automation/

# --- caches ---
.openhands/cache/

# --- lock files (fcntl targets, see persistence/store.py `_file_lock`) ---
.openhands/.settings.lock
.openhands/.secrets.lock
.openhands/agent-profiles/.agent-profiles.lock
.openhands/profiles/.profiles.lock
.openhands/meta-profiles/.meta-profiles.lock

# --- atomic-write temp files ---
# `_atomic_write_json` writes a sibling temp file before the rename; a crash
# between the two leaves it behind.
.openhands/*.tmp
.openhands/**/*.tmp

# --- Tier 3 runtime ---
# The SDK falls back to <workspace>/.openhands for the ACP credential root and
# the npm cache when a conversation is not persisted (acp_agent.py:2528, 2535).
# Normal persisted conversations never land here, but the fallback exists.
project/acp/
project/npm-cache/
